# Typed Vulkan ABI constants, named after the Khronos registry entries.
import lib/std.dl

in this file, by default:
    numbers are 32 bit

the Vulkan instance create info tag means: 1
the Vulkan device queue create info tag means: 2
the Vulkan device create info tag means: 3
the Vulkan submit info tag means: 4
the Vulkan memory allocate info tag means: 5
the Vulkan fence create info tag means: 8
the Vulkan semaphore create info tag means: 9
the Vulkan buffer create info tag means: 12
the Vulkan image create info tag means: 14
the Vulkan image view create info tag means: 15
the Vulkan shader module create info tag means: 16
the Vulkan pipeline shader stage create info tag means: 18
the Vulkan pipeline vertex input state create info tag means: 19
the Vulkan pipeline input assembly state create info tag means: 20
the Vulkan pipeline viewport state create info tag means: 22
the Vulkan pipeline rasterization state create info tag means: 23
the Vulkan pipeline multisample state create info tag means: 24
the Vulkan pipeline depth stencil state create info tag means: 25
the Vulkan pipeline color blend state create info tag means: 26
the Vulkan pipeline dynamic state create info tag means: 27
the Vulkan graphics pipeline create info tag means: 28
the Vulkan pipeline layout create info tag means: 30
the Vulkan sampler create info tag means: 31
the Vulkan descriptor set layout create info tag means: 32
the Vulkan descriptor pool create info tag means: 33
the Vulkan descriptor set allocate info tag means: 34
the Vulkan write descriptor set tag means: 35
the Vulkan framebuffer create info tag means: 37
the Vulkan render pass create info tag means: 38
the Vulkan command pool create info tag means: 39
the Vulkan command buffer allocate info tag means: 40
the Vulkan command buffer begin info tag means: 42
the Vulkan render pass begin info tag means: 43
the Vulkan image memory barrier tag means: 45
the Vulkan swapchain create info khr tag means: 1000001000
the Vulkan present info khr tag means: 1000001001

the Vulkan transfer source buffer usage means: 1 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan uniform buffer usage means: 16 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan vertex buffer usage means: 128 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan transfer destination image usage means: 2 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan sampled image usage means: 4 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan depth stencil image usage means: 32 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan host visible memory flag means: 2 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan host coherent memory flag means: 4 as an unsigned integer
the Vulkan host visible coherent memory flags means: (the Vulkan host visible memory flag) bitwise or (the Vulkan host coherent memory flag)
the Vulkan sampled transfer destination image usage means: (the Vulkan sampled image usage) bitwise or (the Vulkan transfer destination image usage)
